WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.013
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.313 --> 00:00:08.851
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.151 --> 00:00:13.881
Unit twelve: Shopping. Today you will tell a story about a shopping trip.

4
00:00:14.181 --> 00:00:16.822
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:21.127
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:21.983 --> 00:00:22.683
Mall.

7
00:00:23.683 --> 00:00:26.170
Mall means a large building with many shops.

8
00:00:26.783 --> 00:00:28.144
We went to Aeon Mall.

9
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.915
Your turn. Say: Mall.

10
00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:34.628
Mall.

11
00:00:35.383 --> 00:00:36.164
Bargain.

12
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:39.765
Bargain means something bought for a low price.

13
00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:41.955
These shoes were a bargain!

14
00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:44.750
Your turn. Say: Bargain.

15
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:48.322
Bargain.

16
00:00:49.083 --> 00:00:49.864
Fitting room.

17
00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.918
Fitting room means a small room where you try on clothes.

18
00:00:54.517 --> 00:00:56.470
I tried the jeans in the fitting room.

19
00:00:57.083 --> 00:00:59.840
Your turn. Say: Fitting room.

20
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:03.655
Fitting room.

21
00:01:04.417 --> 00:01:05.336
Cashier.

22
00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:09.093
Cashier means the person who takes your money in a shop.

23
00:01:09.683 --> 00:01:11.102
I paid the cashier.

24
00:01:11.717 --> 00:01:14.114
Your turn. Say: Cashier.

25
00:01:16.967 --> 00:01:18.026
Cashier.

26
00:01:18.783 --> 00:01:19.575
Receipt.

27
00:01:20.583 --> 00:01:23.326
Receipt means a paper that shows what you paid.

28
00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.127
Keep your receipt.

29
00:01:25.717 --> 00:01:28.392
Your turn. Say: Receipt.

30
00:01:31.233 --> 00:01:32.200
Receipt.

31
00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:34.183
Exchange.

32
00:01:35.183 --> 00:01:38.390
Exchange means to give something back and get a different one.

33
00:01:38.983 --> 00:01:41.482
I exchanged the shirt for a bigger size.

34
00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:44.875
Your turn. Say: Exchange.

35
00:01:47.733 --> 00:01:48.990
Exchange.

36
00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:50.600
Sale.

37
00:01:51.617 --> 00:01:53.988
Sale means a time when prices are lower.

38
00:01:54.583 --> 00:01:56.409
There's a big sale this weekend.

39
00:01:57.017 --> 00:01:59.297
Your turn. Say: Sale.

40
00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:03.018
Sale.

41
00:02:03.783 --> 00:02:04.645
Budget.

42
00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:08.927
Budget means the amount of money you plan to spend.

43
00:02:09.517 --> 00:02:11.389
My budget is twenty dollars.

44
00:02:11.983 --> 00:02:14.276
Your turn. Say: Budget.

45
00:02:17.133 --> 00:02:17.833
Budget.

46
00:02:18.583 --> 00:02:19.817
Impulse buy.

47
00:02:20.817 --> 00:02:23.919
Impulse buy means something you buy suddenly without planning.

48
00:02:24.517 --> 00:02:26.725
The sunglasses were an impulse buy.

49
00:02:27.317 --> 00:02:29.783
Your turn. Say: Impulse buy.

50
00:02:32.633 --> 00:02:34.052
Impulse buy.

51
00:02:34.817 --> 00:02:35.818
Discount.

52
00:02:36.817 --> 00:02:39.710
Discount means money taken off the normal price.

53
00:02:40.317 --> 00:02:42.699
Students get a ten percent discount.

54
00:02:43.283 --> 00:02:46.005
Your turn. Say: Discount.

55
00:02:48.867 --> 00:02:49.833
Discount.

56
00:02:50.583 --> 00:02:51.805
Loyalty card.

57
00:02:52.817 --> 00:02:56.035
Loyalty card means a card that gives you points when you shop.

58
00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:58.870
I use my loyalty card at the bookshop.

59
00:02:59.483 --> 00:03:02.403
Your turn. Say: Loyalty card.

60
00:03:05.267 --> 00:03:06.628
Loyalty card.

61
00:03:07.383 --> 00:03:08.303
Checkout.

62
00:03:09.317 --> 00:03:11.850
Checkout means the place where you pay in a shop.

63
00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:14.391
The checkout line was long.

64
00:03:14.983 --> 00:03:17.682
Your turn. Say: Checkout.

65
00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:21.488
Checkout.

66
00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:25.986
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.407
Visal, did you go shopping last weekend?

68
00:03:30.517 --> 00:03:33.503
Yes, I went to the mall with my cousin.

69
00:03:34.617 --> 00:03:35.966
Did you buy anything?

70
00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:41.328
I found a great bargain. The sneakers had a fifty percent discount!

71
00:03:42.417 --> 00:03:43.847
Did you stay on budget?

72
00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:49.683
Almost! I bought a cap too. It was an impulse buy.

73
00:03:50.833 --> 00:03:52.090
Part three: grammar.

74
00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:56.052
Grammar focus: Past simple narrative.

75
00:03:56.352 --> 00:03:57.609
Look at the pattern.

76
00:03:58.317 --> 00:03:59.620
I went to the mall.

77
00:04:00.517 --> 00:04:02.191
I found a great bargain.

78
00:04:03.083 --> 00:04:05.106
After that, I paid at the checkout.

79
00:04:06.067 --> 00:04:12.582
Many common verbs are irregular: go → went, find → found, buy → bought, pay → paid.

80
00:04:13.317 --> 00:04:16.944
Be careful! Don't say: I buyed a new bag.

81
00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:20.633
Say: I bought a new bag.

82
00:04:20.933 --> 00:04:23.118
'Buy' is irregular: buy, bought.

83
00:04:23.933 --> 00:04:26.319
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:28.285
A Great Bargain.

85
00:04:28.585 --> 00:04:32.129
Last Saturday, I went to the mall with a budget of thirty dollars.

86
00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:36.712
There was a big sale, so I found a great bargain on sneakers.

87
00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:40.977
I tried some jeans in the fitting room, but they didn't fit.

88
00:04:41.967 --> 00:04:46.277
At the checkout, the cashier gave me a discount with my loyalty card.

89
00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:50.334
I kept the receipt in case I needed to exchange anything.

90
00:04:51.433 --> 00:04:55.249
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:04:56.083 --> 00:04:58.106
Last week, I blank a new bag.

92
00:04:58.406 --> 00:05:01.630
A, bought. B, buy. C, buyed.

93
00:05:05.167 --> 00:05:06.690
The answer is A: bought.

94
00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:10.256
A paper that shows what you paid is a blank.

95
00:05:10.556 --> 00:05:14.233
A, receipt. B, budget. C, sale.

96
00:05:17.767 --> 00:05:19.859
The answer is A: receipt.

97
00:05:21.017 --> 00:05:23.690
Money taken off the normal price is a blank.

98
00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:27.817
A, discount. B, bargain. C, checkout.

99
00:05:31.367 --> 00:05:33.262
The answer is A: discount.

100
00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:37.688
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.863
Describe your last shopping experience.

102
00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:51.185
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:51.485 --> 00:05:59.852
Last month, I went to Psar Thmei with my mother. I bought a new school bag. It was a bargain, and I stayed on budget.

104
00:06:00.152 --> 00:06:01.780
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:02.683 --> 00:06:06.764
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and past simple narrative.

106
00:06:07.064 --> 00:06:11.562
Today's value is saving wisely. Save a little money and spend it carefully.

107
00:06:11.862 --> 00:06:14.700
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.536
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

